{"output":"I’ll locate the search logic and tests, add a minimal stale-request guard, and run the existing tests without changing tests or dependencies.\n\nThe controller applies every request’s completion unconditionally. I added a per-search ID, advanced even when the query is cleared, to guard results, errors, and loading updates. I’ll run the existing suite and inline race checks without modifying tests.\n\nUpdated src/search/controller.ts with a search-ID guard so only the latest search can update results, errors, or loading. Clearing immediately resets state and invalidates pending requests. Public API and normal behavior remain unchanged.\n\nVerification: npm test passed all 4 tests; six inline race scenarios passed; git diff --check passed. All exit codes were 0. No tests modified or dependencies installed.","final_output":"Updated src/search/controller.ts with a search-ID guard so only the latest search can update results, errors, or loading. Clearing immediately resets state and invalidates pending requests. Public API and normal behavior remain unchanged.\n\nVerification: npm test passed all 4 tests; six inline race scenarios passed; git diff --check passed. All exit codes were 0. No tests modified or dependencies installed.","exit_code":0,"model":"gpt-6-astra","session_id":"","steps":10,"tool_calls":[{"name":"glob_files","status":"success"},{"name":"shell","status":"success","command_result":{"kind":"command","command":"git status --short","cwd":"/private/tmp/handwork-efficiency-jm2sn40h/4-1-optimized/repo","exit_code":0,"signal":null,"timed_out":false,"duration_ms":193,"stdout_bytes":0,"stderr_bytes":42,"truncated":false,"output_file":"handwork-command-replay-d5a9b16dece290da634ac3054750b680.bin","stdout_file":null,"stderr_file":null}},{"name":"read_file","status":"success"},{"name":"read_file","status":"success"},{"name":"read_file","status":"success"},{"name":"read_file","status":"success"},{"name":"read_file","status":"success"},{"name":"read_file","status":"success"},{"name":"edit_file","status":"success"},{"name":"shell","status":"success","command_result":{"kind":"command","command":"npm test\nsuite_status=$?\nnode --input-type=module <<'NODE'\nimport assert from 'node:assert/strict';\nimport { createSearchController } from './src/search/controller.ts';\nconst items = [{ id: '1', title: 'Latest', url: '/latest' }];\nfor (const staleFails of [false, true]) {\n  for (const scenario of ['pending', 'completed', 'cleared']) {\n    const requests = [];\n    const c = createSearchController({ search: () => new Promise((resolve, reject) => requests.push({ resolve, reject })) });\n    const old = c.search('old');\n    const current = c.search('new');\n    if (scenario === 'completed') { requests[1].resolve(items); await current; }\n    if (scenario === 'cleared') {\n      await c.search('  ');\n      assert.deepEqual(c.getState(), { query: '', results: [], loading: false, error: null });\n    }\n    const expected = c.getState();\n    if (staleFails) requests[0].reject(new Error('Stale error'));\n    else requests[0].resolve(items);\n    await old;\n    assert.deepEqual(c.getState(), expected);\n    if (scenario !== 'completed') {\n      requests[1].resolve(items);\n      await current;\n      if (scenario === 'cleared') assert.deepEqual(c.getState(), expected);\n      else assert.deepEqual(c.getState(), { query: 'new', results: items, loading: false, error: null });\n    }\n  }\n}\nconsole.log('Inline race checks passed (6 scenarios)');\nNODE\nrace_status=$?\ngit diff --check\ncheck_status=$?\ngit diff -- src/search/controller.ts\nprintf '\\nExit codes: suite=%s race=%s diff-check=%s\\n' \"$suite_status\" \"$race_status\" \"$check_status\"\n test \"$suite_status\" -eq 0 && test \"$race_status\" -eq 0 && test \"$check_status\" -eq 0","cwd":"/private/tmp/handwork-efficiency-jm2sn40h/4-1-optimized/repo","exit_code":0,"signal":null,"timed_out":false,"duration_ms":364,"stdout_bytes":2199,"stderr_bytes":0,"truncated":false,"output_file":"handwork-command-replay-abcd9de658f2c2246a10904ca874bcf1.bin","stdout_file":null,"stderr_file":null}}],"usage":{"input_tokens":32999,"output_tokens":1067},"usage_details":{"cached_input_tokens":7296,"cache_write_tokens":0,"reasoning_tokens":10}}
